EXT. DUSTY SALOON PORCH, CROSSROADS TOWN - NOON

A single street of plank buildings baking in white sun. A water trough. A hitching rail. Tumbleweed rolls by, unhurried, and fetches up against a barrel.

On the porch sit two men. SHERIFF AUGUSTUS BRANDYWINE-OKORO (50s, graying mustache, tin star) rocks in a chair with a tin cup of coffee. Beside him, DEPUTY TOBIAS "TOBY" FAIRWEATHER-LIN (20s, too-new hat, a rifle across his knees) whittles at a stick.

SHERIFF
Quiet today.

TOBY
Always quiet on Wednesdays.

SHERIFF
Quiet's a good thing.

TOBY
Yes, sir.

SHERIFF
Quiet's also a warning.

TOBY
Yes, sir?

SHERIFF
Quiet means somebody's up to something.

TOBY
Or nobody is.

SHERIFF
Son, the nobody's the one to worry about.

Toby considers this. Sets down the stick.

TOBY
Should I go look?

SHERIFF
Look at what?

TOBY
Anything.

SHERIFF
Sit down.

TOBY
I am sitting.

SHERIFF
Sit down harder.

A horse snorts somewhere behind the livery. A shutter bangs. The two men go still.

TOBY
(whispering)
Sheriff.

SHERIFF
I heard it.

TOBY
Was it the wind?

SHERIFF
Might've been.

TOBY
Might not.

SHERIFF
Might not.

Boots on gravel. A new figure rounds the corner of the general store: MADELEINE VOSKUIJLEN-ADEOLA (30s, dust-colored duster, wide-brimmed hat, a carpetbag in one hand, spurs that sing). She stops in the middle of the street and looks at the porch.

MADELEINE
Afternoon, gentlemen.

SHERIFF
Ma'am.

TOBY
Ma'am.

MADELEINE
I'm looking for the sheriff.

SHERIFF
You've found him.

MADELEINE
I've a letter for you.

SHERIFF
From who?

MADELEINE
(together)
From Judge Hollis in Santa Rita.

TOBY ^
(together)
Judge Hollis in Santa Rita?

SHERIFF
Toby.

TOBY
Sorry, Sheriff.

Madeleine sets down the carpetbag. Pulls a folded envelope from her coat. Holds it up between two fingers. Neither man moves.

MADELEINE
Shall I bring it up, or will you come down?

SHERIFF
Bring it up.

She mounts the steps. Hands him the letter. He reads. Reads again. Folds it. His face goes still.

SHERIFF (CONT'D)
(low)
Toby. Go inside.

TOBY
Sheriff?

SHERIFF
Go inside and lock the door.

TOBY
What's it say?

SHERIFF
Just do it.

Toby rises, the chair scraping, and goes into the saloon. The door closes. A bolt drops. Madeleine and the Sheriff stand alone on the porch with the wind and the tumbleweed.

SHERIFF (CONT'D)
It says there's a man coming.

MADELEINE
There is.

SHERIFF
It says he's coming for me.

MADELEINE
He is.

SHERIFF
It says you're his sister.

Madeleine tilts her head. A long silence. The wind lifts the brim of her hat.

MADELEINE
He's not coming for you, Sheriff. I am.
